WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
1. Review the connected account
Choose Cloud and confirm the intended provider and region.
This account already has a CryoStack access role. Select Review connection setup to inspect the saved connection.
Account identifiers are hidden in this tutorial.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:28.000
2. Inspect the existing setup
Review current AWS connection keeps the existing connection and saved role.
Review existing AWS stack opens its template, permissions and Outputs RoleArn for inspection.
The AWS-console inspection is explained here; it is not recorded in this clip.

3
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:48.000
First connection: AWS setup
For a new connection: Connect AWS Account → Open AWS Setup → review the role template and permissions → create the stack.
Copy Outputs RoleArn back into CryoLauncher, then select Verify connection.
These first-time creation steps are explained, not performed. This recording reuses an existing role.

4
00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:04.000
3. Use the same saved role
Copy or paste the saved Role ARN for this same connection. Then select Verify connection.
To connect a different account, use Change AWS account rather than replacing the role in this review form.
The role is masked. Entry and verification were completed during an omitted wait.

5
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:20.000
4. Confirm actual verification
The recorded final state says: Verified the existing connection. No new access role was created.
Verification uses fresh temporary access and checks the AWS account identity.
This confirms account access. It does not prepare compute resources, test MATLAB or check billing.

6
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:36.000
5. Continue to the run review
Connected and the updated Last verified time confirm the saved account is usable. Select Done to close the review.
Check storage, compute, image and any MATLAB readiness before launching.
BYO runs charge the connected AWS account. The run estimate is separate from AWS Billing.

